          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On the night of August 15 to 16, 2004, a man observing from his balcony saw, twice, golden, sparkling lights moving at high speed in a clear sky. First, at approximately 03:50, the lights moved in a triangle formation; second, at 04:20, they were in a straight line, following the same trajectory as before. Note the proximity to Lille Lesquin Airport. No further information could be gathered about this observation, which was classified as C.",
